  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Prompt Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the prompt! I\'m meticulously analyzing every requirement to ensure no detail is overlooked. The goal is a comprehensive understanding of every feature, section, detail, and styling element for a truly meticulous build. I\'m focusing on dissecting specifications to ensure complete alignment.\n\n\n**Defining Brand Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to solidify SK Texture\'s brand identity. I\'ve noted the company name, tagline, and contact information. Now, I\'m defining the design language \342\200\223 aiming for a luxurious minimalist aesthetic akin to Apple, Porsche, and leading architectural firms. I\'m focusing on color palettes, typography choices, and the type of imagery to be used. I\'m also planning the animations and UI to ensure a premium look.\n\n\n**Visualizing Architectural Textures**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual elements. I see the site showcasing premium architectural surfaces \342\200\223 plaster, stone, microcement, and the like. The hero section is taking shape with a full-screen video, toggleable controls, and impactful text overlays. I\'m already imagining a trust metrics bar to build confidence. The action buttons are taking shape: \"Get Free Site Visit\" and \"Explore Catalogue\".\n\n\n**Detailing Service Specifications**\n\nI\'m now detailing the services section! I\'m emphasizing my experience in Gurugram, Delhi NCR, and nationwide. I\'m showcasing exterior wall textures, decorative stone coatings, and thermal/waterproofing expertise. The client base includes prominent firms like DLF, M3M, and Tata Housing. Highlighting my commitment to craftsmanship, durability, weather resistance, and eco-friendliness is key.\n\nI am also considering an interactive texture spec comparison table, and interactive layering diagrams. Now, I am structuring the services section with architectural cards and hover animations, featuring custom vector icons. I\'m planning to include marble, rustic, concrete finish, granules, parlina, brick textures, and a super finish.\n\n\n**Expanding Catalogue Options**\n\nI\'m expanding the texture catalogue, envisioning an Apple-inspired layout with masonry grids and zoom interactions. I am adding fine roller, super fine spray, and compact textures. I\'m incorporating waterproofing and heat-reflective coatings, plus exterior painting services. I\'ve also detailed interior texture finishes, and commercial/villa specialities. I\'m structuring a robust interactive filter and search system by category.\n\n\n**Refining Texture Presentation**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the texture catalogue display. I am creating Apple-style, full-screen modals triggered by click-throughs. Each modal will have crisp images and a color selector. I\'m focusing on texture names, finish feel descriptions, applications, color swatches, and maintenance instructions. I am ensuring that interior, exterior, and both use tags are included. I\'m also adding \"Request Sample\" buttons.\n\n\n**Designing Project Displays**\n\nI\'m now designing the \"Projects\" section to be a strong showcase! I\'m planning a Pinterest-style masonry layout with comprehensive filters: Residential, Commercial, Schools, Hospitals, Builders, Apartments, and Luxury Villas. Each interactive project card will feature an \"interactive before-after slider\" to display the dramatic transformation from plain walls to SK Texture\'s finished masterpieces. I\'m focusing on providing details like location, builder name, area covered, products used, completion date, and a verified customer review.\n\n\n**Defining Key Company Attributes**\n\nI\'m now identifying core value pillars and company strengths to reinforce the brand\'s premium positioning. I\'m focusing on highlighting the extent of projects completed, nationwide services, premium materials, expert application, and extreme weather resistance. I\'m noting the 10+ year warranty, and thermal insulation benefits for added value.\n\n**Curating Client Testimonials**\n\nI am now designing the client testimonials section! I\'m creating luxury cards with high-resolution photos, builder badges, architect quotes, 5-star ratings, and location indicators. I\'m ensuring diverse testimonials from various clients: builders, architectural firms, villa owners, and facility directors.\n\n**Assembling a Visual Gallery**\n\nI\'m developing an inspiring gallery! I\'m planning a Pinterest-style masonry photo display of completed luxury projects, featuring villas, apartment facades, brick textures, and commercial towers. I\'m including hover zoom animations and a Lightbox view for full image viewing and texture details.\n\n\n**Constructing Feature Specifications**\n\nI\'m now detailing an intuitive process timeline, broken down into numbered steps for the user. I\'m also planning interactive tools: a texture visualizer for wall renders, an AI cost estimator, and an expansive FAQ section for user inquiries. I\'m focusing on the user experience and ease of navigation to keep engagement high.\n\n\n**Implementing Contact Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial contact methods. This includes a phone dial link and a WhatsApp chat link. I\'m also adding an instant quote request form with file upload, date picker, and image preview. I\'m focusing on user-friendly accessibility.\n\nI am also making a sticky header, which will contain: glassmorphic top navigation bar, quick phone call, theme toggle, and the primary \"Book Free Site Visit\" button. I plan to use a bottom-right floating WhatsApp button with quick message pre-fill, as well as a quick phone button. I am implementing a smooth theme toggle with custom dark and light themes. A comprehensive footer with navigation, copyright, social links, schema metadata, and address details is being added.\n\nFinally, I\'m working on sourcing high quality assets to give the website the Apple/Porsche/Architectural Digest look and feel. I will use `generate_image` or source high-resolution architectural images.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 369581213
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
