  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Visual Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on the user feedback, specifically their suggestion that the previous design was \"good\" but not \"that much good.\" This means a comprehensive review and refinement of the visual elements is critical. I\'m prioritizing improvements in the color palette, typography hierarchy, contrast, spatial rhythm, and the interactive elements\' polish throughout the site.\n\n\n**Analyzing Luxury Website Designs**\n\nI\'ve been auditing what makes luxury websites visually compelling, drawing inspiration from Apple and architectural studios. I\'m focusing on color palettes that evoke warmth and sophistication: creams, limestone, and deep mineral charcoals, with bronze and gold accents. I\'m also considering a dark mode with velvet mineral blacks and warm graphite. Specifically for the hero section, I\'m integrating dynamic background selectors and material specifier badges to elevate the user experience.\n\n\n**Developing Visual Structure**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the visual hierarchy, choosing Cormorant Garamond for headlines with italic accents and Plus Jakarta Sans for body text. I\'m also implementing a high-impact statistics bar with gold hairline dividers. I\'m focusing on the *TextureCatalogue.tsx*, aiming for an Apple product gallery or high-end material archive look with filtering, search, and a zoom-in texture inspect modal with detailed specs.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Functionality**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing interactive features, particularly for a textured surface visualizer. I\'m focusing on dynamic controls for material selection (e.g., Cement, Warm Ochre, Charcoal Slate), lighting angle adjustments (Sunlight, Evening Ambient), and real-time wall depth renderings. A live spec sheet summary with a \"Get Quote\" button will be integrated.\nI\'m also considering interactive before/after sliders, filterable portfolios, architectural project cards, and a dynamic cost estimator.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 461215720
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
