    thinking: "**Envisioning Aesthetic Transformation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on transforming the application into a world-class architectural masterpiece. My initial approach involves organizing the design upgrades component by component, starting with the brand palette and global aesthetics.\n\n\n**Defining the Visual Language**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously defining the visual language, starting with a refined palette. I\'m focusing on \"Cream\", \"Mineral Off-White\", \"Sandstone\", \"Deep Charcoal\", and \"Obsidian\" as base colors, complemented by \"Muted Warm Gold\" and \"Crisp Hairlines.\" I\'ve also selected Cormorant Garamond, Syne, and Serif Editorial for display headlines, and Plus Jakarta Sans and Mono for subtitles, UI, and specifications. I\'m aiming for glassmorphism, gold grain overlays, and tactile finishes.\n\n\n**Detailing Technical Specifications**\n\nI\'m now detailing technical specs and interactive elements. The \"About\" section will feature a 4-Coat Stack Visualizer. It will explain each layer with specs and cross-section diagrams. The services section will include cards for each architectural offering with toggles for inspecting specs and mockups.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Visualizers**\n\nI\'m now diving into the development of interactive visualizers. I plan to create a texture catalogue using an Apple Product Page/material specimen gallery layout, complete with filter tabs and search functionality for high-resolution texture cards. I\'m also working on an interactive \"Wall Studio,\" which will allow users to customize scenes and surfaces in real-time. My main focus is providing detailed spec modals for each texture, including coat thickness, turnaround time, substrate compatibility, and real project photo examples.\n\n\n**Expanding Interactive Features**\n\nI\'m now expanding the interactive features, specifically focusing on the projects showcase. I\'m prioritizing an interactive before/after slider within categorized filters and full case study details in a modal view. I\'m also developing a cost and surface calculator with real-time estimates and a comparison matrix to highlight the value proposition of my textures. My goal is to enhance user engagement and provide clear, accessible information. I\'m focusing on user-friendly interactivity.\n\n\n"
